- **Original Code:** `student.EnrollmentDate > new DateTime(9999, 12, 31)`
- **Mutation:** `student.EnrollmentDate > new DateTime(9999, 12, 30)` OR `student.EnrollmentDate >= new DateTime(9999, 12, 31)`
- **Why it survives:** Tests only validate MinValue/default check and an out-of-range date (1700s), but never test the exact upper boundary (9999-12-31). Boundary shifts wouldn't be detected.
- **Recommended fix:**
  ```csharp
  [Fact]
  public void Create_POST_ExactUpperBoundaryDate_IsValid()
  {
