#### 9. **DeleteConfirmed - Missing Null Check Before Access**
- **Location:** `/tmp/sv-903c1ed848d849d7a050306979bfd987/ContosoUniversity/Controllers/CoursesController.cs`, line 210-211
- **Original Code:** `Course course = db.Courses.Find(id); var courseTitle = course.Title;`
- **Mutation:** Remove null safety check; if course is null, accessing `.Title` throws NullReferenceException
- **Why it survives:** Test only deletes an existing course. No test attempts to delete a non-existent course that would fail.
- **Recommended fix:**
  ```csharp
  [Fact]
  public void DeleteConfirmed_NonexistentId_HandlesGracefully()
  {
      var controller = CreateController(context);

      // Should not throw; should handle gracefully
      var result = controller.DeleteConfirmed(99999);

      // Verify it either redirects or returns a result without crashing
      Assert.NotNull(result);
  }
  ```

---

#### 10. **Index - Include Chain Validation Gap**
- **Location:** `/tmp/sv-903c1ed848d849d7a050306979bfd987/ContosoUniversity/Controllers/CoursesController.cs`, line 33
- **Original Code:** `var courses = db.Courses.Include(c => c.Department);`
- **Mutation:** Remove `.Include(c => c.Department)` → Departments not eagerly loaded
- **Why it survives:** Test asserts `Assert.All(model, c => Assert.NotNull(c.Department))` BUT this doesn't definitively prove eager loading vs. lazy loading (if lazy loading is enabled). If the mutation removes Include, test passes as long as navigation property is accessed during the loop.
- **Recommended fix:**
  ```csharp
  [Fact]
  public void Index_DepartmentsEagerlyLoaded()
  {
      // Create course with department
      var dept = CreateTestDepartment(99, "Test Dept");
      context.Departments.Add(dept);
      var course = CreateTestCourse(9999, "Test", 99);
      context.Courses.Add(course);
      context.SaveChanges();

      using var controller = CreateController(context);
      var result = controller.Index() as ViewResult;

      var model = Assert.IsType<List<Course>>(result.Model);
      var course1 = model[0];

      // Clear change tracker to simulate detached context
      context.ChangeTracker.Clear();

      // Accessing Department should NOT require new DB query (proves eager load)
      Assert.NotNull(course1.Department);  
      Assert.Equal("Test Dept", course1.Department.Name);
  }
  ```

